] [17592186361829 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186361829 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "de8be4ac-d669-50ad-ba32-f79a71f23b2c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186361870 #edb/ref 1080 "2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186361870 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186361870 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "e75d0f27-b8bb-5a5c-8905-034c15c6f3c9" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186361917 #edb/ref 1080 "1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186361917 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186361917 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "f250f6bc-6c44-51cf-a2c2-612e5c87a588" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186361932 #edb/ref 1080 "1-\\sqrt{2}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186361932 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186361932 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "f466069f-33e0-5fe4-9e0d-eb960bf7ce61" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186361949 #edb/ref 1080 "-11" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186361949 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186361949 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "f8bff70f-6e8b-5be6-916a-ad154e650d51" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186361959 #edb/ref 1080 "16" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186361959 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186361959 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "faf4cd0b-f3f9-5c75-a7ea-835686f7d019" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186362031 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186361357 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186362031 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186361581 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186362031 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186361671 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186362031 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186361870 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186362031 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186361959 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186362031 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186362031 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186362031 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186361959 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186362031 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "314fa88d-8f92-5297-95d3-76a7ddb9d25f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186362032 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186361147 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186362032 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186361192 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186362032 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186361573 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186362032 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186361829 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186362032 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186361949 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186362032 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186362032 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186362032 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186361949 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186362032 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "34c90b2e-8911-5c08-acf8-00710f4117fa" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186362125 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186361250 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186362125 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186361429 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186362125 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186361514 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186362125 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186361917 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186362125 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186361932 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186362125 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186362125 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186362125 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186361429 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186362125 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "9b70f22b-a5a8-585e-b3dd-fa50d2c97d20" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186365213 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186365214 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186365213 #edb/ref 1069 "q-162765" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186365213 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186365213 #edb/ref 1071 "Use the method of Lagrange multipliers to find the maximum value of the function $f(x,y)=1-{x}^{2}-3{y}^{2}\\,$ on the ellipse $2{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}-2y=0.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186365213 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "c36493f2-f6b8-5f91-9602-a932566cf19e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186365213 #edb/ref 1074 "We must find the maximum value of $f(x,y)$ subject to the constraint $g(x,y)=2{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}-2y=0.$ \n\nSince $f(x,y)$ is continuous and the constraint is closed and bounded, $f(x,y)$ reaches a global maximum and a global minimum on the constraint. \n\nTherefore, by the method of Lagrange multipliers, we must solve the following system:\n\n$$\n∇f(x,y)=\\lambda ∇g(x,y),\\,g(x,y)=0\n$$\n\nWe start by solving the first equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x,y) & =\\lambda ∇g(x,y) \\\\ ⟨{f}_{x}(x,y),{f}_{y}(x,y)⟩ & =\\lambda ⟨{g}_{x}(x,y),{g}_{y}(x,y)⟩ \\\\ ⟨-2x,-6y⟩ & =\\lambda ⟨4x,2y-2⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-2x &=4\\lambda x \\\\ -6y &=2\\lambda (y-1)\\end{aligned}\\right.\\,⇒\\,\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x(1+2\\lambda ) &=0 \\\\ y(\\lambda +3) &=\\lambda\\end{aligned}\\right.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo solve this system, we break it up into several cases:\n\n- Assuming $x=0$ in the first equation of the system, the constraint condition $2{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}-2y=0$ implies\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{2}-2y & =0\\,⇒\\,y=0,2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis gives the critical points $(0,0),(0,2).$\n\n- Assuming $\\lambda =-\\frac{1}{2}$ in the first equation of the system, the second equation of the system implies\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(-\\frac{1}{2}+3)=-\\frac{1}{2}\\,⇒\\,y=-\\frac{1}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, the constraint condition $2{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}-2y=0$ implies\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{x}^{2}=-\\frac{11}{25}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich gives a contradiction.\n\nTherefore, $f$ has possible extreme values at the points\n\n$$\n(0,0),\\,(0,2).\n$$\n\nWe evaluate $f$ at these points. These are given in the following table:\n\n| $(x,y)$ | $(0,0)$ | $(0,2)$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $f(x,y)$ | $1$ | $-11$ |\n\nTherefore, the function reaches a maximum value at the point $(0,0)$ and its maximum value is $1.$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186365214 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186365215 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186365214 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186365216 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186365214 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186365217 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186365214 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186365218 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186365214 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186365219 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186365214 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186365214 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186365214 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186365218 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186365214 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "30f4541b-0d8a-526a-afe2-a9aa2ea8fd81" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186365215 #edb/ref 1080 "9" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186365215 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186365215 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "0c1a9567-a313-551f-8955-ecaba2978cde" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186365216 #edb/ref 1080 "11" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186365216 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186365216 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "6db71774-d7fa-5f78-a1ef-b5912f624201" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186365217 #edb/ref 1080 "8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186365217 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186365217 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "77dfb2d7-3549-503d-8180-ec857c5d2c33" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186365218 #edb/ref 1080 "1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186365218 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186365218 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "9899ec02-9b96-560f-a1cc-1d5024d0846e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186365219 #edb/ref 1080 "5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186365219 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186365219 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "40291836-4e30-51b2-ae65-ae6465fdf18d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186365226 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186365227 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186365226 #edb/ref 1069 "q-162792" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186365226 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186365226 #edb/ref 1071 "Use the method of Lagrange multipliers to find the maximum value of the function $f(x,y,z)={z}^{2}-{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}$ on the paraboloid ${x}^{2}+{z}^{2}-y=0.$\n\n*Hint: You may assume that the global maximum of $f(x,y,z)$ exists on the surface.*" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186365226 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "c6ff3f5a-d486-56fd-99cb-379dcba19a45" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186365226 #edb/ref 1074 "We need to find the maximum value of $f$ subject to the constraint $g(x,y,z)={x}^{2}+{z}^{2}-y=0.$ Therefore, by the method of Lagrange multipliers, we must solve the following system:\n\n$$\n∇f(x,y,z)=\\lambda ∇g(x,y,z),\\,g(x,y,z)=0\n$$\n\nWe start by solving the first equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x,y,z) & =\\lambda ∇g(x,y,z) \\\\ ⟨{f}_{x}(x,y,z),{f}_{y}(x,y,z),{f}_{z}(x,y,z)⟩ & =\\lambda ⟨{g}_{x}(x,y,z),{g}_{y}(x,y,z),{g}_{z}(x,y,z)⟩ \\\\ ⟨-2x,-2y,2z⟩ & =\\lambda ⟨2x,-1,2z⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe start by solving the first equation:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-2x &=2\\lambda x \\\\ -2y &=-\\lambda \\\\ 2z &=2\\lambda z\\end{aligned}\\right.\\,⇒\\,\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}(1+\\lambda )x &=0 \\\\ y &=\\frac{\\lambda }{2} \\\\ (1-\\lambda )z &=0\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nTo solve this system, we break it up into several cases:\n\n- First, assume that $\\lambda \\ne \\pm 1.$ Then, by the first and third equations, we must have $x=z=0.$ Also, by the constraint $g(x,y,z)=0,$ we have\n\n$$\ny={0}^{2}+{0}^{2}\\,⇒\\,y=0.\n$$\n\nThis gives the critical point $(0,0,0).$\n\n- Next, assume that $\\lambda =-1.$ Then, by the second and third equations, we must have $y=-\\frac{1}{2}$ and $z=0,$ but this contradicts the constraint $g(x,y,z)=0.$\n\n- Finally, assume that $\\lambda =1.$ Then, by the first and second equations, we must have $x=0$ and $y=\\frac{1}{2}.$ Also, by the constraint $g(x,y,z)=0,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{2}={0}^{2}+{z}^{2}\\,⇒\\,z=\\pm \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}.\n$$\n\nThis gives the critical points $(0,\\frac{1}{2},\\pm \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}).$\n\nWe evaluate $f$ at each of these points. These are given in the following table:\n\n| $\\,(x,y,z)\\,$ | $\\,(0,0,0)\\,$ | $\\,(0,\\frac{1}{2},\\pm \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}})\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\,f(x,y,z)\\,$ | $\\,0\\,$ | $\\,\\frac{1}{4}\\,$ |\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\nTherefore, the function reaches a maximum value at the points $(0,\\frac{1}{2},\\pm \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}),$ and its maximum value is $\\frac{1}{4}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186365227 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186365228 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186365227 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186365229 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186365227 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186365230 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186365227 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186365231 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186365227 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186365232 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186365227 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186365227 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186365227 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186365230 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186365227 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "3bd3adff-ea86-59fd-bc52-90fe39fade8a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186365228 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{1}{2}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186365228 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186365228 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "c067ceed-329e-51d4-8634-a1d0a81bb476" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186365229 #edb/ref 1080 "2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186365229 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186365229 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "e75d0918-e0c0-5785-afab-223f2739e64f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186365230 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{1}{4}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186365230 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417]